    <item>
      <title>Airlive Bridge 1.4.0</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>18</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.4.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[Auto Cut: a new AUTO button beside CUT switches between cameras that have a picture, holding each shot for a random time inside your range, and any manual cut hands control back to you. Bridge can also be driven from Stream Deck through the upcoming Airlive plugin. The top bar wraps to a second row on narrower windows instead of letting controls overlap.]]></description>
      <enclosure
        url="https://github.com/airlive-project/airlive-bridge/releases/download/v1.4.0/Airlive-Bridge-1.4.0.dmg"
        length="11393066"  type="application/octet-stream"
        sparkle:edSignature="OiUefWljmVZ61ITRacKtT0pKNmpdjtwnrNiroNK7HN0MlJx4WSjffDHaahMjUSEtszIGCSmvIoaDq45kV7x2CA==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Airlive Bridge 1.3.1</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>17</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[A channel could get stuck advertising itself as occupied while nothing was connected to it, which left it unreachable from every phone. A phone is also given longer before it counts as dead, so a live camera is not dropped over an ordinary Wi-Fi gap.]]></description>
      <enclosure
        url="https://github.com/airlive-project/airlive-bridge/releases/download/v1.3.1/Airlive-Bridge-1.3.1.dmg"
